    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "K depletion (common): freq serum K monitoring; tx prn w PO or parenteral KCl"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hemodialysis: for renal failure and sometimes for ethylene glycol, methanol or salicylate poisoning"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Type 4 RTA: a few pts need mineralocorticoid replace (fludrocortisone 0.05 to 0.2 mg PO once/day); caution, may worsen HTN, HF or edema"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "RTA bone dz: vitD (eg, ergocalciferol 800 IU PO once/day) and PO Ca supp may be needed to help reduce skeletal deformities from osteomalacia or rickets"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
